  <!-- Art wired 2026-09-20 from `rot_mycoidcolossus_v2_{south,east,north}`, rendered
       2026-09-19 under ROT_FLORA_FAUNA_VERDICTS_1 and approved by the owner on sight
       ("That's a cool mycoid. I like it."). 2048px masters downscaled to 1024 with
       premultiplied alpha; the sub-visible export halo (alpha 1-16, ~80k px per facing)
       was zeroed first, taking measured fringe from 2.1% to 0.85%.
       1024 is deliberate, not a shortfall: at the ruled drawSize the 128 px/cell target
       lands past what the generator fills with real detail, so this ships at ~85 px/cell,
       the same call the sea-beast colossi shipped at.
       HISTORY: this mod previously carried a DROID, mis-routed here by the bulk install
       cea007c3a. Those renders were kept, not deleted, at
       src/RimStarWars/Droidworks/ArtIncoming/ on the owner's word.
       ⚠️ MEASURED and NOT fixed, because it is a cosmetic call that is his: north's
       subject is 922x981 (aspect 0.94) against south 983x656 and east 1003x671 (aspect
       ~1.50), so at one drawSize box north draws about half again as tall as the other
       two facings. That is the same "north is HUGE compared to east" defect he named on
       Anooba. Recomposing north would change the art, so it waits on his word. -->
  <description>Replaces sarg.alphaanimals's AA_MycoidColossus art (adult lifeStage look, south/east/north
facings only - any alternate-skin or dessicated-corpse textures stay on donor
art) with an invented-recast render generated for this campaign. LABEL/ART
ONLY - no defName touched, no Defs, no Patches, loose Textures/ only, same
relative path (Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_MycoidColossus/AA_MycoidColossus_&lt;facing&gt;) the donor uses so this mod's later
load order wins the same-path resolution.</description>
  <loadAfter>
    <li>sarg.alphaanimals</li>
  </loadAfter>
</ModMetaData>
